{
  "_comment": "P0 contract fixture for the deadline-alert reader. This is the shape the RN app writes to users.data['hs-tracker-data'] (a 6-bucket object; here inlined as an object rather than the JSON-string the client stores, and test_deadline_alert_reader.py json.dumps() it back to that form). Authored from frontend/src/api/trackerStore.ts + status.ts — SYNTHETIC, no real user data (this base is largely minors). Dates are RELATIVE placeholders resolved at test time by day-offset tokens like '+3' so the fixture stays valid forever; the test replaces each '${...}' token. Every item exercises one rule of the reader; the expected units are asserted item-by-item in the test. Any change to the tracker shape must update this file — that is what surfaces the server-side impact.",

